"Positions daily observations in a calendar grid so weekday and seasonal patterns are visible.\n\nUse when: Each observation belongs to a date and calendar position matters. Daily patterns, missing days, or recurring weekday differences need inspection.\n\nAvoid when: Precise numeric differences or irregular noncalendar intervals are the main question.\n\nVisual grammar: Cell position encodes week and weekday within a labeled calendar. Cell fill encodes the daily value using a labeled sequential or diverging scale.\n\nBuild: Generate every date in the declared calendar window, including missing days. Place weeks and weekdays consistently and label month boundaries. Apply a shared color scale and render missing days distinctly from zero.\n\nCheck: Check weekday placement, leap days, and week-boundary conventions. Verify the daily aggregation and time zone are explicit. Confirm all years or panels use compatible color domains.\n\nPitfalls: Calendar gaps are missing observations, not necessarily zero activity. Month borders must avoid obscuring cell values or tiny day labels.\n\nExample: Show synthetic daily library visits over one year with week columns, weekday rows, and a clear count legend.\n\nAlternatives: Lasagna plot, Seasonal subseries plot, Line chart."
